; libOPNMIDI XG: GM percussion (notes 35-81) from five percussion banks.
; MIT: Copyright (c) 2018-2026 Vitaliy Novichkov.
; See licenses/libopnmidi-xg.txt and README.md.
; Each drum is an FM voice whose :key is the bank's fixed key: written for
; :oct 4, play c; other notes retune it. The standard kit is fm-<role>; the
; other kits add only the drums that sound different, as fm-<kit>-<role>.
; Drums with the same registers extend the first.

; ---- Standard kit (StandKit): bank "XG #001 StandKit", MSB 0 / LSB 0 ----

; GM 35 kick2: * BassDrum
(def-fm fm-kick2 :key 35 :alg 2 :fb 4 :ams 0 :fms 0
  :ar1 27 :dr1  0 :sr1 20 :rr1 7 :sl1  0 :tl1   0 :ks1 0 :ml1 0 :dt1 0 :ssg1 0 :am1 0
  :ar2  0 :dr2 15 :sr2 12 :rr2 6 :sl2 15 :tl2 127 :ks2 0 :ml2 6 :dt2 0 :ssg2 0 :am2 0
  :ar3  0 :dr3 11 :sr3 15 :rr3 5 :sl3 15 :tl3 127 :ks3 0 :ml3 5 :dt3 0 :ssg3 0 :am3 0
  :ar4 31 :dr4  0 :sr4 14 :rr4 7 :sl4  0 :tl4   0 :ks4 1 :ml4 1 :dt4 0 :ssg4 0 :am4 0
)

